options strategies, unit investment trusts, institutional money managers, and no-load multi-manager variable annuities. In addition, the company offers retirement solutions for commission and fee-based services that allow advisors to provide brokerage services, consultation, and advice to retirement plan sponsors. Further, it provides other services comprising tools and services that enable advisors to maintain and grow their practices; trust, investment management oversight, and custodial services for estates and families; an advisor-facing trading and portfolio rebalancing platform; insurance brokerage general agency services; and technology products, including proposal generation, investment analytics, and portfolio modeling. The company was formerly known as LPL Investment Holdings Inc. and changed its name to LPL Financial Holdings Inc. in June 2012. LPL Financial Holdings Inc. was founded in 1989 and is based in San Diego, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Richard  Steinmeier | CEO & Director | Age 51 | Compensation: $4.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 10K people. Revenue per employee of $1.6M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 12%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $8K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["LPL Financial Holdings Inc. is a large-cap financial services business with a $23.0B market cap on $17.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +25% over the past three years and +15% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 17% against a 8% cost of capital, a 8-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The company is burning through $982M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 4.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 2.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 6.7% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 69% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.69031657280958},{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 22% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Accruals running hot at +6.9% of assets \u2014 earnings quality bears watching","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $2.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["13 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"LPL Financial Holdings Inc. $LPLA Shares Newly Bought by Provenance Wealth Advisors LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/lpl-financial-holdings-inc-lpla-shares-newly-bought-by-provenance-wealth-advisors-llc.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793877920.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.955,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is LPL Financial Holdings (LPLA) Undervalued On Strong Q3 Earnings And Dividend News?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nasdaq-lpla/lpl-financial-holdings/news/is-lpl-financial-holdings-lpla-undervalued-on-strong-q3-earn","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793863919.759,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.893,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","dividend"]},{"title":"Does Earnings Turnaround Change The Bull Case For LPL Financial Holdings (LPLA)?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nasdaq-lpla/lpl-financial-holdings/news/does-earnings-turnaround-change-the-bull-case-for-lpl-financ","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793770363.017,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.71,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Recent Research Analysts\u2019 Ratings Changes for LPL Financial (LPLA)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/03/recent-research-analysts-ratings-changes-for-lpl-financial-lpla.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793753807.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.052,"tier":0,"scope":"company","ta